{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/653789-swarm-form-how-close-to-beast-s-skin","id":653789,"title":"Swarm Form: How Close To Beast's Skin?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-06T06:12:29-07:00","id":653789,"title":"Swarm Form: How Close To Beast's Skin?","content":"The rules are a little unclear as to just how much of the Beast's Skin elements you use when calculating stats for a Kindred using the Swarm Form merit, so I just want to ask step by step just which parts remain as per the Beast's Skin level of Protean, and which do not.<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes and Skills: </b>Do we use the Kindred's attributes and skills, or do we use those of the animal in question as per Beast's Skin? The part which mentions the Kindred moving at a speed calculated as per Kindred's original speed, with the animal's size factored in, so the lack of reference to the other stats pertaining to size makes me wonder if that was intentional, and the Attributes remain those of the Kindred with the merit, but I would like to be sure.<br /> <br /> <b>Health: </b>Usually calculated as Size+Stamina, I a curious if the health is supposed to be that of the Kindred with the merit, or Size of animal+Stamina of the Kindred? Suppose it could be read as being the size of the Kindred, otherwise a swarm could likely be very easily wasted with the right amount of damage against a low stamina Kindred, but again, would like to be sure.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1353-riche","name":"RichE","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T08:03:03-07:00","id":653920,"title":"","content":"I assume Beast's Skin is irrelevant to Swarm Form outside of being a prerequisite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T09:17:42-07:00","id":653985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/653789-swarm-form-how-close-to-beast-s-skin?p=653920#post653920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume Beast's Skin is irrelevant to Swarm Form outside of being a prerequisite.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I would assume the opposite. Since Swarm form is worded &quot;when using Beast's Skin, some Gangrel can instead become a swarm of small creatures&quot; and then goes on to explain the special rules for swarms, my assumption would be that the power uses the normal rules for Beast's Skin, except where Swarm Form specifically says otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T11:58:45-07:00","id":654214,"title":"","content":"The reason I assume the opposite is because Beast's Skin doesn't allow some of the creatures Swarm Form does so wasn't designed for tiny critters and a swarm of rats is very different than a rat in their effect. You don't get attacked by 10 different rats, it would be a group of 10 rats attacking in unison. The wording is a little confusing. It talks about armor and other modifiers to defend the swarm. I've never heard of animals having armor ratings outside of a horse wearing actual armor. As I haven't used it, I think the real answer would be how does it work best. I do not know. Somebody should run it with rats and some kind of insects to see how it goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T12:18:31-07:00","id":654229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/653789-swarm-form-how-close-to-beast-s-skin?p=654214#post654214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason I assume the opposite is because Beast's Skin doesn't allow some of the creatures Swarm Form does so wasn't designed for tiny critters and a swarm of rats is very different than a rat in their effect. You don't get attacked by 10 different rats, it would be a group of 10 rats attacking in unison. The wording is a little confusing. It talks about armor and other modifiers to defend the swarm. I've never heard of animals having armor ratings outside of a horse wearing actual armor. As I haven't used it, I think the real answer would be how does it work best. I do not know. Somebody should run it with rats and some kind of insects to see how it goes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, those are all places where Swarm Form specifies that it works differently than Beast's Skin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T15:26:13-07:00","id":654492,"title":"","content":"I imagine that Swarm Form doesn't use the normal rules for Beast's skin because the result is rather extremely mediocre if it does. Among other things, the resulting STR + Brawl roll is never going to be higher than 1. Also, we don't actually have stats for bugs, which are an option for Swarm Form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T15:42:25-07:00","id":654496,"title":"","content":"Maybe my first response was taken too literal. I would assume the kindred's stats are used for everything except for the odd case where merits and skills are inapplicable due to the creatures making up the form being unable to use them and abilities of the creature making up the form are granted when they are a function of the form.<br /> <br /> Take the case of a bat which has stats in the World of Darkness book: strength 1, brawl 1, health 2. Using the animals stats gives you a swarm that is really weak. Even with just one damage per hit, you're toast after four hits. You get to bypass defense, which is nice, but you only get to divide damage from that pitiful 2 dice pool among targets in a swarm that can be spread 5 yards per blood potency. Using the kindred's stats makes everything seem more relevant. Of course, if you need to make a roll for flying then go ahead and use the Athletics (Flight) 4.<br /> <br /> \u200bI guess it would still be fair to say it works like Beast's Skin except where it is suggested that it doesn't, but then the suggestion exists for just about everything, except senses and movement type. I don't know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T18:17:40-07:00","id":654618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/653789-swarm-form-how-close-to-beast-s-skin?p=654496#post654496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe my first response was taken too literal. I would assume the kindred's stats are used for everything except for the odd case where merits and skills are inapplicable due to the creatures making up the form being unable to use them and abilities of the creature making up the form are granted when they are a function of the form.<br /> <br /> Take the case of a bat which has stats in the World of Darkness book: strength 1, brawl 1, health 2. Using the animals stats gives you a swarm that is really weak. Even with just one damage per hit, you're toast after four hits. You get to bypass defense, which is nice, but you only get to divide damage from that pitiful 2 dice pool among targets in a swarm that can be spread 5 yards per blood potency. Using the kindred's stats makes everything seem more relevant. Of course, if you need to make a roll for flying then go ahead and use the Athletics (Flight) 4.<br /> <br /> \u200bI guess it would still be fair to say it works like Beast's Skin except where it is suggested that it doesn't, but then the suggestion exists for just about everything, except senses and movement type. I don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you considering the fact that you can still use vigor when in swarm form? Maybe your swarm form is supposed to be weak, but when you add the passive and, most of all, active effects of vigor it starts to get interesting when you get to bypass defence.<br /> <br /> But there are indeed a lot of wierd things:<br /> For starters is not exactly quite clear HOW the speed is modified. Does it change the species factor? Is it a bonus to total speed? A negative? A multiplier?<br /> Then, WHY being in swarm form should let you consider the strenght, dexterity and, if (see above), the species factor of the human form? A swarm of rats should be on average as fast as a single rat...<br /> Also, since a swarm is clearly bigger than a single animal, why does the health of a single rat and a swarm of rats should be unchanged? I can figure that if you get in single rat form and someone waves a big knife at you, it can cut you in half, so that's why both the stamina and the size result in a really small health pool: in rat proportions, the damage is massive. But a swarm is quite a lot of little things you can cut in half, so even if the stamina of the single animal is what it is, the size of the swarm should factor in the total health pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2213,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2213-tittopaolo210","user":"TittoPaolo210","date":". 09-06-2015, 09:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2213-tittopaolo210","name":"TittoPaolo210","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T19:36:54-07:00","id":654675,"title":"","content":"Speed is the same as vampire minus the difference in size between vampire and base creature forming swarm. Speed is Size + Strength + Dexterity + Vigor. In this case, the vampires stats are clearly used. &quot;The swarm moves at the vampire\u2019s Speed, modified for the creatures\u2019 Size...&quot; I would use the kindred's stats to represent the health pool of the swarm. It doesn't matter how much health an individual member of the swarm has. The swarm has a number of members to represent the kindred's health. A swarm of rats would certainly be stronger than a single rat. A swarm can move things around. You can use vigor with Beast's Skin too. A swarm of rats is still limited when it comes to physical actions, as would a normal group of rats. A swarm couldn't swing a sword or fire a gun, for instance. Kindred stats makes sense to me. It isn't a swarm of animals following the orders of one mind. It is a swarm of animals with the same mind. Like a multiple core processor, simultaneous actions can process faster at slower speeds. I can live with Swarm Form being much stronger than Beast's Skin as it is a supplement on top of Beast's Skin. YMMV<br /> <br /> Many weird things indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}